WEBVTT

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.880
Shogi Club

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.880
Urushi Yaotome

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.880
Ayumu Tanaka

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.630
You've gotten a lot better,
but you've still got a long way to go.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.420
I'm just amazed, Senpai. You're so good at shogi.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.460
I know. I know.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.630
And you're so cute, too.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.960
You have a crush on me, don't you?

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.580
What are you talking about?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.960
Well, come on! You joined the shogi club,
and I'm the only member!

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.540
I wanted to play shogi.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.920
But you knew nothing about the game!

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.000
I still wanted to play.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.500
And then you just call me cute to my face.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:16.880
You are cute.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.290
The little turd! He just refuses to admit it!

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.750
In that case...

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:29.500
If you admit that you have a crush on me,
I'll give you a hug.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.880
Not enough for him, eh? Okay...

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.880
And I... I'd be willing... to give you a kiss.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.500
Senpai. I'm trying to concentrate.
Would you mind being quiet please?

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:58.960
That was close.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.540
I almost caved and blurted out the truth.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.170
I'm sorry, Senpai.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.540
I swore to myself that I wouldn't tell you that
I like you until after I've beaten you at shogi.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:10.830
And so...

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.750
I declare right here and now that I will win this game.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:19.540
In your dreams, stupid!

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.710
There. It's over.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.330
I... I didn't know you could do that.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:01.250
KING

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.790
Yeah, right, like I'd ever let you finish
your Bear-in-the-hole castle.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.580
Game 1: You Are Cute, Senpai

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.670
I said this to you before, but maybe
you should try focusing a little more on offense?

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.710
All you ever do is defend.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.500
Offense?

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.580
I just feel like defense is more my style.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:22.750
Really? But you're always so aggressive.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.130
What do you mean, I'm "always so aggressive"?

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.040
Uh, well, how can I put it...?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.080
Like, do you have any examples?

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.080
There's an example right there!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:41.130
These things that embarrass the crud out of me
are constantly coming out of his mouth...

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:44.380
Dangit... It's about time I embarrassed him for once!

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.790
I'll counterattack by telling him how handsome he is!

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.670
By... by the way...

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.880
Now that I really look at you, you're pretty h... h...

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.500
H... hand...

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.710
Han... hand...

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.380
You know what, never mind!

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.250
So what did you mean when you said I'm aggressive?

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:17.920
PAWN

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.880
W-well, you know...

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:21.630
You say things that embarrass me,
like... calling me cute...

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.540
I wouldn't call that aggressive. I'm just telling the truth.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:27.250
TRUTH

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:31.080
How can this guy have such a strong offense!?

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.380
Senpai.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.710
He's already on his next attack?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.420
Not good, not good, not good!

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.750
I'm going to crumble under his onslaught...

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.540
I give up--you win.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.040
S-see, didn't I tell you?

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:57.500
You really need to study up on your offensive strategies.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.250
Yes, Senpai. I'll do my best.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.920
Urushi!

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:12.750
Maki.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.630
You're in an awfully good mood.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.330
I guess so.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.080
Going to club?

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:19.750
Yup.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.080
See you later.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:25.750
Buh-bye! See you tomorrow!

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:38.290
Promoted pawn, promoted pawn.
Once promoted, pawns are strong.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:43.080
Unpromoted pawns are strong,
but put two together and you lose!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.080
No, seriously, dude.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.420
We have to win our next tournament! We just have to!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.830
And you're the Immovable Tanaka,
unshakable as a mountain! Right?

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:53.540
Back in middle school,
you were so good, you were famous!

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.210
No, I'm not that good.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:58.460
So come on, man. Please join the kendo team!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.540
Anyway, you'll at least think about it, right?

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.790
We'll welcome you onto the team, anytime you're ready!

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:16.000
Senpai?

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.250
Wh-what a coincidence!

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.420
Fancy meeting you here!

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:21.830
Uhh...

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:24.330
Club... Were you going to shogi club?

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.580
We can go together!

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:34.880
So, Sen...

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.080
Uh, oh yeah!

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.500
You have gotten a lot better.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.830
So today I'll let you use the champion King
instead of the challenger King!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:45.170
You did say you thought
the champion King was cooler, right?

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.330
No, the challenger King is fine.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.290
Since I still haven't managed to beat you.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:57.000
O-okay, then I'll play with the 2-piece handicap!
Then you can...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.170
It doesn't mean anything unless I win fair and square.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.170
Oh...

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.710
So... Hey.

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:18.420
Senpai.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.330
You have nothing to worry about.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.290
I'm not going to join the kendo team.

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:29.540
Really!?

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.630
Uh, I mean... I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.290
Oh, that's okay.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.830
Actually, Senpai, is it okay if
I use the champion King after all?

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.130
Well, if you must. But only for today.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.880
Shogi Club

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.880
Urushi Yaotome

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.880
Ayumu Tanaka

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:58.920
I wasn't ready. I'm still not fit to use the champion King.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.750
But you did pretty well that time.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.920
What's going on? Did you get some good news?

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:14.290
Uh-huh!

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:17.330
Seeing you happy makes me happy, Senpai.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.500
Oh, does it? Heh heh.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:21.790
Guess what!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.540
We're getting a new club member today!

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.460
A new... club member...?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.750
I invited one of my classmates,
and she just texted to let me know she's on her way!

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.580
You wanted... members...

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.460
You wanted new club members, Senpai?

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.380
Yeah. Of course.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.210
May I ask why?

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.710
Well, I want to make this a club.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.500
It wasn't already a club?

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.830
Shogi Club

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.830
Urushi Yaotome

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.830
Ayumu Tanaka

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:51.880
I mean...

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.460
I put that up there myself. It's not official.

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:58.000
We just need two more members
before we're a real club.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:01.420
Oh, but now we only need one...

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:04.790
Senpai, why exactly do you want to make this a club?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:10.710
Uh... well... because "shogi club" has a... nice ring to it?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.290
A nice ring to it?

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:17.460
But is it necessary? I mean, we're already
technically calling ourselves the shogi club.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.290
Hm, that's true.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:21.290
To get club funds, then!

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:24.710
We have everything we need, don't we?

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:27.580
What point is there in getting club funds
if we're not going to use them for anything?

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.710
For a club room, then.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:33.460
Is this room not good enough? I mean...

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.000
Hey, wait a minute!

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.170
You're acting kinda weird! Are you attacking me!?

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.290
No, I only want to make things clear.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.080
I know!

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.920
If we get more members,
you might be able to beat someone!

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:49.290
I'm always destroying you--surely
you'd like to win once in a while!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.630
No, I...

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.330
Oh, she's here!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.210
Let me introduce you!

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.420
This is our newest member, Goto...

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.330
I'm so sorry!

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:00.710
I found a boyfriend, so I'm gonna have to quit shogi.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.250
I'm sure you understand.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.920
Wow, Senpai. That's a real shame.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:13.380
Why do you look so happy?

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:15.250
Did I look happy?

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:17.920
Yes, you did! What is wrong with you?

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:27.380
But seriously. Just because she has a boyfriend?

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:29.460
No...

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:32.710
I guess normally, people would put their boyfriend first.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.170
Not that I'd really know.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:38.500
If you ever got a boyfriend, Senpai,
would you still come to club?

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:42.580
You know I'd never quit. I love shogi.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.750
Besides, I'm the club president.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:46.250
But we're not a club.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:47.710
Stop nitpicking.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:49.080
I'm sorry.

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:56.130
KING

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:02.750
What about you?

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:05.380
If you get a girlfriend...

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.710
Would you stay in the shogi club?

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.170
If I got a girlfriend...

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.880
Actually, I think I'd hang out at club even more.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.000
Because I want to play shogi
with you for the rest of my life.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.960
Suddenly he's practically proposing to me!

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:32.790
Based on the way you said that, it kind of sounds
like the "girlfriend" you have in mind is me...

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.460
I think you might be imagining things.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.130
Oh, I get it now!

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:41.460
You're against having new club members
because they would ruin your alone time with me!

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:45.250
I knew it. You do have a crush on me.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.500
Checkmate.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.920
No, there should still be something I can do.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.040
No, it's checkmate! In the game and
our conversation! Admit defeat!!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:03.040
When Will Ayumu

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:03.040
Make His Move?

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:09.130
Hey, hey.

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:09.670
Mm-hm?

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:11.040
Have you tried the new sandwich from the student store?

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:11.960
Oh! No, I haven't.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:14.210
It's the triple sesame-miso-yakisoba sandwich.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:15.580
I hate this.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.000
Senpai. What's wrong?

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.920
Huh? What are you doing here?

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.920
You were walking with a very spring-less step,
so I followed you.

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:28.830
What are you, a stalker?

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:29.920
So? What's the matter?

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:36.330
Well, I have P.E. next, but I hate P.E.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.420
I have no athletic ability.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:44.130
Hm, yeah, you are always tripping over nothing.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:50.880
And you have misjudged the distance and jammed your
finger in the locker when you went to get your shoes.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:55.830
And hopped up and down in front of a vending machine
when you couldn't reach the button.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.290
How do you know about all these things?

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:04.130
I don't think it will be easy to give you any surefire tips
to help you instantly improve your athletic functions.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.250
I'm sorry.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:10.040
Don't look at me like that!
You're making me want to do this even less!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.500
So... you want to just blow it off?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:19.920
I'll go somewhere with you.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.460
Oh, I don't know. Skipping class would just be...

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:27.790
I'd rather have you, you know, try to cheer me up.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.920
Cheer you up, Senpai?

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:36.460
You won't need a lot of athletic ability in your life--
you're cute enough to get by without it.

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:40.960
Your smile is cuter than anything.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:45.000
But when you have that serious look
on your face, you're very pretty.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:50.500
Your hair is nice and shiny, your cheeks
are like freshly peeled boiled eggs...

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.290
And your fingernails are as lovely as little pink seashells.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.290
And...

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.000
Stop, stop, stop!

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:01.080
Did that cheer you up?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.790
Ch-cheer me up...?

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:08.080
No, you're actually... making it worse.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.670
What are you going to do, Senpai?

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:22.540
I guess I really will skip it. With you.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.540
I'm okay with that.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.130
O-on second thought, I'll go to P.E.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:37.920
Really? Well, good luck.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:44.580
See you after school!

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:48.830
Yeah.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:01.250
Shogi Club

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:01.250
Urushi Yaotome

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:01.250
Ayumu Tanaka

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.250
Senpai.

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:03.380
Today, I will be beating you.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.630
Really. Do you have some kind of secret strategy?

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:28.500
No. You wouldn't. Is this...

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.500
The invincible castle?

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.500
Such a weak strategy.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:39.750
What? It's weak?

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.080
But it's invincible!

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.710
Why would you try to construct that castle?

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:47.880
Because... I saw the word "invincible"
and it got me all excited.

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:52.460
I know how you feel, but...

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:53.920
You say it with a straight face!

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:55.380
What are you, in fourth grade?

00:16:59.040 --> 00:16:59.960
Sorry.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:01.580
I shouldn't have laughed that hard.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.460
It's okay.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.670
You're not mad?

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:07.630
No. Actually, I'm happy that I got to see you smile.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:11.830
And knowing that I'm the one who gave you that smile...

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:13.170
I'm in heaven.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:18.630
Because your smile is really beautiful.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.880
He's doing it again!

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.290
I know!

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.750
I'll build an invincible castle around my heart!

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:40.130
Allow me to teach you about the invincible castle.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:42.290
Yes, I am here to learn.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:46.500
First, it's easy to build, and you can finish it super fast.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.830
And it's a strong defense against any frontal attack.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:52.290
Senpai, you know everything. I'm so impressed.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:53.830
You have my respect.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.000
But this castle has a weakness.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:02.630
I just came up with this "invincible heart castle" idea off
the top of my head, but it's working pretty well.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.380
It is truly invincible!

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:08.170
It's this: if it is attacked from the side, it's practically
worthless.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:24.000
It's hard to see what you're saying from
the other side of the board. May I watch from here?

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:32.920
KING

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:45.670
You see? It's weak... against side attacks...

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:47.040
You're right.

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:51.170
Anyway, do you want to play another game?

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:52.130
Absolutely!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:05.500
Check!

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:07.750
There's no beating you.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.420
You're definitely getting better, but you're going
to need to do more tsume shogi puzzles.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.880
I'll have some recommendations for you next time.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:23.580
But you'll make a good impression with that
straightforward offensive strategy.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:25.290
Straightforward, Senpai?

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:29.710
On the other hand, maybe you could afford
to be a little more devious.

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.210
Thank you for all your help.

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:35.920
I'm happy to know that you're thinking about me.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:41.130
Of course I am. I'm your senpai.

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:45.170
So... it's raining.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.420
It... it sure is.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.960
Senpai. Did you bring an umbrella?

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:54.290
An umbrella?

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.170
Yeah, I brought one.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:59.080
Just a little folding one, but it's still pretty sturdy.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.080
Um... Would you like to share
my umbrella on the way home?

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:08.880
What... do you mean by that...?

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:10.500
Exactly what I said?

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.380
Did you listen to me? I told you I have my own!

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.920
Is that a no?

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:21.880
I know! I can take his straightforward attack,
and turn it against him!

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:27.790
Well, if you insist on strolling under
an umbrella with me, I suppose I wouldn't mind.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:29.330
Take that! Who's turning red now!?

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.250
Yes. I do insist on strolling under
an umbrella with you, Senpai.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:36.580
That's too straightforward!

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.250
Well, okay, then.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:10.960
It... it's raining pretty hard, huh?

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.040
Yeah.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.380
Do you think the sun will be out tomorrow?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.630
I hope it rains again tomorrow.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:27.080
He's so nice to me...

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:32.420
Oh, my house is...

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:33.460
This way, right?

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.420
Huh? How do you know?

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:37.830
I looked it up once.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:39.580
What? That's creepy!

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:42.920
Senpai.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.040
Thank you for today.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:50.750
I'm really happy that I got to share an umbrella
with the senpai I have so much respect for.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:53.580
Uh, urgh.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:59.880
K-keep going straight from here.

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:02.580
Then if you take the second right, and the first left...

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:08.330
There's an okonomiyaki place a little past there.
Do you know it?

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:10.750
No. Is it any good?

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:12.880
It's good. Really good.

00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:14.250
That sounds nice.

00:22:14.630 --> 00:22:15.420
Doesn't it?

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:16.630
Yes.

00:22:25.420 --> 00:22:30.130
If it means that much to you,
we could do this... again sometime...

00:22:30.790 --> 00:22:32.080
Share an umbrella, I mean.
